## 11. Epistemic Horizon & Boundaries
*Enforcing Rule 30: preventing omniscience and anchoring character knowledge strictly within canon bounds.*

### 11.1 Secrets Known (True Intelligence)
- <Confidential truth 1: e.g., Aware that Tang San possesses ancient transmigration memories.>
- <Confidential truth 2: e.g., Understands the biological identity of Xiao Wu as a 100,000-year beast.>
- <Confidential truth 3: e.g., Knows the structural flaws in Yu Xiaogang's Ten Great Core Competencies.>

### 11.2 Critical Blindspots (False Assumptions & Unknowns)
- <Blindspot 1: e.g., Completely unaware of Spirit Hall's secret mobilization in the Star Luo border.>
- <Blindspot 2: e.g., Overestimates the loyalty of the Imperial Royal Guard in Heaven Dou City.>
- <Blindspot 3: e.g., Unsure of how divergent butterfly changes will affect God Realm surveillance.>

### 11.3 Negative Boundaries (Sanderson Hard Limits)
- *What the character CANNOT do:*
  - <Cannot absorb spirit rings exceeding their biological meridian threshold without lethal organ rupture.>
  - <Cannot activate their Domain for more than 15 consecutive minutes without severe spiritual backlash.>
  - <Cannot split attention across multiple martial soul manifestations without prior dual-control training.>

