## 14. Standardized Lexicon & Taxonomy Glossary

| Term / Taxonomy | Category | Clear & Accessible Definition |
|:---|:---|:---|
| **Aura / Bearing (*Qizhi*)** | Demeanor | The intangible aesthetic weight, psychological posture, and ambient presence projected by a cultivator (e.g., sharp as a drawn sword, serene as ancient jade, or tyrannical). |
| **Dao Heart (*Daoxin*)** | Psychology | The core philosophical bedrock and moral resolve of a character. When fractured by betrayal or failure, leads to bottleneck stagnation or mental collapse. |
| **The Ghost** | Psychology | A formative past trauma, loss, or displacement that generates a lingering fear and psychological vulnerability. |
| **The Lie Believed** | Psychology | A false survival rule or rationalization adopted in response to the Ghost, which limits character growth until challenged by the plot. |
| **Sanderson Sliders** | Psychology | Three numerical 1–10 axes evaluating **Likeability** (audience empathy), **Competence** (skill and effectiveness), and **Proactivity** (initiative). |
| **Innate Soul Power** | Cultivation | The baseline soul power level (Rank 1 to 10) discovered during the Awakening ceremony at age 6, determining lifelong cultivation ceiling. |
| **Spiritual Power Realm** | Cultivation | Six cognitive-mental tiers measuring soul awareness and sensory precision: Spirit Origin (1-100), Spirit Connection (101-500), Spirit Sea (501-5k), Spirit Abyss (5k-20k), Spirit Domain (20k-50k), and Divine Origin (50k+). |
| **Soul Core (*Hunhe*)** | Cultivation | A condensed vortex of high-density energy formed in the Dantian, Chest, or Sea of Consciousness upon reaching high cultivation ranks (Rank 80+). |
| **Martial Soul Avatar** | Power | The supreme manifestation unlocked with the 7th Spirit Ring, transforming the master into the living physical embodiment of their martial soul for a +100% stat boost. |
| **External Spirit Bone (*Waifuhungu*)** | Anatomy | Rare anomalous spirit bones outside the 6 standard slots (e.g., spider legs, wings) that evolve alongside the host's personal cultivation breakthroughs. |
| **Battle Armor (*Doukai*)** | Equipment | Fusion of spiritually refined metals, soul guidance circuits, and bloodline resonance (1-Word to 4-Word) acting as an external technological exoskeleton. |
| **Epistemic Horizon** | Continuity | The strict boundary of what a character actually knows versus what they assume, preventing authorial omniscience and maintaining believable character choices. |

